WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.440
ANDREW HUBERMAN: Welcome to this
20-minute non-sleep deep rest

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.940
protocol.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.790
Non-sleep deep rest
is a powerful tool

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.160
that can allow you to
control the relaxation

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.200
state of your nervous system
and your overall state of mind.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.110
It can restore mental
and physical vigor,

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:26.100
and it can be done any
time of day or night.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.490
It can even partially offset
the negative consequences

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.700
of getting too little sleep.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.000
Non-sleep deep rest takes
advantage of the fact

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.910
that specific forms
of breathing place us

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:45.070
into a state of deep relaxation
by slowing our heart rate down.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.040
It also takes
advantage of the fact

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.830
that we can control
our perception--

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:55.350
that is, which sensations
we are focused on.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.510
Sensations are
simply the conversion

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:01.200
of physical events in
the world into a language

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.510
that our body and
brain can understand.

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:08.780
It's a process by which
things like photons

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.410
of light, mechanical
pressure on our skin,

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:15.590
sound waves, and so
on, are converted

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.960
to electrical and
chemical signals

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:22.400
in our neurons, or nerve cells.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.520
Perception is simply
the sensations

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.940
that we happen to be focused
on at a given moment.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:35.010
And perception is an incredible
aspect of our nervous system.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:38.910
We can't directly control
what sensations are around us

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.600
and inside of us,
they are just there.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.910
But we can control our
two kinds of perceptions.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:51.510
One kind of perception
is called exteroception,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.230
and is when we pay attention
to things around us

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.930
beyond the confines of our skin.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.760
The other type of perception
is called interoception,

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.830
and it's when we pay
attention to things

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.230
at the level of the
surface of our skin

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.510
and inward, inside our body.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.730
With non-sleep deep rest, you
can shift your brain state

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:21.190
from one of thinking, stress,
planning, from anticipation

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:25.150
of any kind, positive
or negative, to one

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:29.900
of pure sensation
and deep relaxation.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.780
It's very simple to do.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.500
You'll want to do this
protocol seated or lying down.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:43.810
So if you're not already seated
or lying down, please do so now.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.760
You'll also want
to close your eyes.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:52.770
So if your eyes aren't already
closed, please close them now.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.170
Throughout this
protocol you'll want

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:59.040
to breathe normally, unless
instructed to do otherwise.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.600
One pattern of breathing
you'll be asked to do

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:08.570
is to Inhale deeply,
ideally through your nose.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.760
But if you can't do
it through your nose,

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.670
inhale through your mouth.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.090
Try that now.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:20.710
Inhale deeply through your nose,
and then exhale all of your air

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:21.535
through your mouth.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.060
Let's do that again.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:35.760
Inhale deeply through your
nose and then exhale completely

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.100
through your mouth.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:42.860
And as you exhale, exhale
through thinly pursed lips

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.540
as if through a small straw.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.530
Let's repeat that
two more times.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:55.410
Inhale deeply through
your nose, and then

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:58.245
exhale completely through
thinly pursed lips.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:05.890
One more time.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:11.030
Inhale deeply through
your nose, and then

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:15.080
exhale completely
through your mouth

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.565
through thinly pursed lips.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:25.240
Breathing in that way,
that is, inhaling deeply

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.540
through your nose and
then exhaling completely

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.880
through the mouth through
thinly pursed lips,

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.747
is known to slow your
heart rate down and relax

00:04:35.747 --> 00:04:36.580
your nervous system.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:43.090
Feel free now to simply
breathe normally.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:51.180
Now, in your mind's
eye, imagine yourself

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:56.160
standing over yourself, looking
at your body which is seated

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.250
or lying down, and
imagine holding

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:06.160
a flashlight or a spotlight
and directing it at your feet.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.720
Focus your attention on whatever
it is that your feet happen

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.120
to be in contact with.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:18.630
It could be socks, sandals,
shoes, or merely the air.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.300
It doesn't matter.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.310
Focus your attention
specifically

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.800
on the bottoms of
your feet, and try

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:30.510
to perceive whatever
it is they are sensing.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.580
They could be tingling.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.260
They could even be numb.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:35.325
It doesn't matter.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:41.590
Now imagine expanding
that spotlight

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:47.660
to include the tops of your
feet, your shins, your calves.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.920
Expanding that spotlight
further to include

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:57.960
your thighs, your hamstrings,
and up to your waist.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:04.840
Now, with your entire
lower body illuminated

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.170
inside the beam of light
from that spotlight,

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:11.410
inhale deeply through your
nose or through your mouth.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:20.660
And then exhale completely
through thinly pursed lips

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.115
until your lungs are empty.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:34.330
Repeat that twice more, and
each time as you exhale,

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:39.240
imagine your lower body
sinking down about a centimeter

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:43.380
into whatever surface you happen
to be in contact with now.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:11.100
Now continue by
breathing normally.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.255
Inhale deeply.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.720
And as you exhale,
imagine your body

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.970
sinking another centimeter
into the surface

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.250
you are lying or
sitting down on.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:38.270
As you inhale, remember to
have your belly expand ever so

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:41.160
slightly.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:47.145
And as you exhale, your stomach
will fall ever so slightly.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.680
As you breathe in
this manner, continue

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:02.915
to imagine the spotlight
illuminating your entire body.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.830
As you Inhale, you can
imagine that spotlight

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:13.150
getting slightly brighter.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:20.120
And as you exhale,
imagine the spotlight

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.440
getting slightly dimmer.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:32.539
Continue to inhale and to
exhale while imagining your body

00:08:32.539 --> 00:08:33.274
sinking down.

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:46.590
Now pay attention to the
muscles of your face.

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:50.190
And as you continue
to breathe normally,

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:54.930
try to relax the
muscles of your face--

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:57.510
at first only slightly.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:05.500
And then with each
subsequent breath,

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:12.045
relaxing the muscles of your
forehead and face more and more.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:32.500
Now, regardless of the
environment you're in,

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:36.550
try to listen to sounds
within that environment.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:43.480
Whatever happens to be
surrounding you, try to hear it.

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:16.500
Perhaps you can only hear the
sound of your own breathing.

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:18.615
Perhaps there are
noises in the room.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:27.030
Regardless of the sounds you
hear, tried to focus on them.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:50.780
Now you will breathe in the
same manner you breathed before,

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:59.800
with a deep inhale through your
nose until your lungs are full.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:06.020
And then a slow, complete exhale
through slightly pursed lips.

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:16.370
Let's repeat that again.

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:21.280
Inhale through your nose
until your lungs are full.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:34.200
Then exhale slowly through your
mouth with slightly pursed lips.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:52.440
Now, in your mind's eye, try
to imagine your body again

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:56.190
illuminated by a spotlight.

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:02.950
Imagine looking
down at yourself,

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:08.830
and your entire body is
illuminated by that spotlight.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:21.540
Dim that spotlight in
your mind by about 50%.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:31.670
And as you do so, deliberately
relax the muscles of your legs.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:45.150
Then deliberately relax
the muscles of your hands,

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:49.865
sensing your palms,
wrists, and fingers.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.245
Continue to breathe normally.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:12.490
And in your mind's eye,
dim the spotlight 50%

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:20.070
further still so that the image
of your body in your mind's eye

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.840
is barely a silhouette.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:48.335
Now, in your mind's eye,
make the spotlight brighter.

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:57.740
Try to see any portion of
your body in your mind's eye--

00:13:57.740 --> 00:14:04.465
your hands, your arms,
your torso, your feet.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:14.900
No matter if you see one or all
of these parts, try to see them

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:17.405
as if you are staring
down at yourself.

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:31.590
Now move the spotlight
to your abdomen

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:34.020
and focus your
attention on whatever

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:36.270
it is your abdomen is sensing.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:44.490
As you inhale, your stomach
should move out slightly.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:47.550
And as you exhale,
it should sink down.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:55.570
Expand the spotlight to
include your upper abdomen,

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:57.850
your chest, your neck.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:04.800
And now in your
mind's eye, imagine

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:08.115
that spotlight is expanding
to include your arms as well.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.010
Continue to breathe normally.

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:18.220
Now focus your
perception on whatever

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:21.670
surface your back happens
to be in contact with--

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:25.800
a shirt, a chair, a sofa.

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:28.380
Whatever surface it
happens to be contacting,

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.510
focus on that contact now.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.500
Simply bring your attention
and your perception

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.650
to those points of contact.

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:46.390
And as you do so, inhale
deeply again through your nose

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:47.410
or through your mouth.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:55.340
And then as you exhale, imagine
your back and your upper body

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:58.700
sinking about a centimeter
into whatever surface

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.350
they happen to be
in contact with.

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.250
Now move the spotlight
to include your face,

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:10.810
the top of your head, and
the back of your head.

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:13.470
And as you continue
to breathe normally,

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:16.200
focus your perception
on relaxing

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:17.745
the muscles of your face.

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:26.450
And as you continue
to breathe normally,

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:29.960
see if you can extend the
duration of your exhales

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.040
ever so slightly.

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:39.230
And now in your mind's eye,
expand the spotlight downward

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:46.380
to include your neck, your
chest, your arms, your abdomen,

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:51.150
your waist, your legs,
and down to your feet.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:03.250
Imagine yourself looking down
at your own body, illuminated

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.530
inside of the spotlight.

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:10.180
And in your mind's eye,
deliberately dim that spotlight.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:12.850
Make the illumination
less intense.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:22.920
Inhale deeply again through
your nose or through your mouth.

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:28.870
And then exhale completely
through thinly pursed lips.

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:33.070
And as you do so,
imagine your entire body

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:36.025
sinking into the surface
it's in contact with.

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:43.980
Now, while continuing
to breathe normally,

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:46.695
move your toes ever so slightly.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:56.420
You'll notice that you are in
control of your nervous system.

00:17:56.420 --> 00:18:01.280
You can direct your
perceptions and your actions.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:03.650
In doing so, you'll
notice that you

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:06.150
are in control of
your nervous system,

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:10.400
meaning you direct your
perceptions and your actions.

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:19.600
Move your ankles and bend your
knees just the slightest bit.

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:22.930
You can move your upper
body from side to side,

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:27.765
your head from side to side,
or even nod just slightly.

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.870
Now move your hands.

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:37.685
Lift your arms just a tiny
bit, then set them down again.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:47.460
And now, whenever you are
ready, slowly open your eyes.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:51.080
And as you do so, you'll
notice that normally

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:55.790
your nervous system is bombarded
with sensory information, mostly

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.450
visual information,
which you have

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:03.850
eliminated during this
non-sleep deep rest protocol.

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:06.250
As you have now
experienced, you are

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:09.100
in control of your perceptions.

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:13.870
Controlling your perceptions is
simply directing your attention

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:17.530
to specific sensations,
and you control

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:21.160
which sensations you
perceive by directing

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:24.430
your attentional
spotlight to whatever part

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:28.500
or parts of your
body that you choose.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:32.790
This reflects the remarkable
power of the human brain.

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:37.700
You can direct your
actions, your perceptions,

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:41.750
and you can do so in order to
bring about deep relaxation.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:48.550
You can also do that to achieve
heightened states of alertness

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:54.475
or attention to any sensation
outside of you, or within you.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:02.350
Non-sleep deep rest
protocols such as this one

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:08.550
can help you restore your sense
of mental and physical vigor,

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:13.800
can partially offset the effects
of not getting enough sleep,

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:21.000
and can also help you get better
at falling and staying asleep.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:24.020
It can be done any
time of day or night

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:28.970
when you feel you need a
mental and/or physical reset.

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:35.880
Thank you for joining me
for this non-sleep deep rest

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:41.480
protocol brought to you
by Huberman Lab and AG1.

